				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/467/347/427/647/201/original/3506ee2939de8823.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-23T16:57:23.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@elk\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>elk</span></a></span> The current logic shows a large preview if the account has a header and the followers count is bigger than 250 or if it wasn't going to be grouped and it has more than 25 followers. I did a heuristic that looked ok but we haven't had time to think much about it. Maybe we should use a percentage of your own followers for example to show big cards to folks that are just starting using Mastodon. You can see the current condition here:<br><a href=\"https://github.com/elk-zone/elk/blob/1a7ae6f0efd6f9cdf5d961328a89574119efae7c/components/notification/NotificationPaginator.vue#L62\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/elk-zone/elk/blob/1</span><span class=\"invisible\">a7ae6f0efd6f9cdf5d961328a89574119efae7c/components/notification/NotificationPaginator.vue#L62</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109739614663736141",
			"parentId": "109739576115025739",
			"url": "https://m.nintendojo.fr/@meduz/109739613897034118",
			"author": {
				"name": "meduz'",
				"url": "https://m.nintendojo.fr/@meduz",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/637/138/050/619/original/298755ab87304007.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-23T17:07:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@patak\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>patak</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@elk\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>elk</span></a></span> Interesting. I would love to have neutrality here: I don’t care about anyone “popularity” that decides to follow me, and the UI as it is now is a bit disturbing for a notification feed. If there’s a setting to have neutrality, I would appreciate it.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
