			},
			"date": "2023-01-23T17:44:44.073Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.social/@jenned\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jenned</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@elk\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>elk</span></a></span> this reply has the full details: <a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@patak@webtoo.ls/109739576115025739\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">fediverse.zachleat.com/@patak@</span><span class=\"invisible\">webtoo.ls/109739576115025739</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109739807907622181",
			"parentId": "109739658845293328",
			"url": "https://m.webtoo.ls/@patak/109739807863527859",
			"author": {
				"name": "patak",
				"url": "https://m.webtoo.ls/@patak",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/467/347/427/647/201/original/3506ee2939de8823.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-23T17:56:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.nintendojo.fr/@meduz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>meduz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@elk\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>elk</span></a></span> Good points. I think if we show the big card expansion for everyone with an avatar and a header it may break your notifications when you do a good post. But I also think it is better if we find an heuristic that doesn't depend on follower count. Maybe we could show it if on top of avatar and header, it has a proper description, and includes at least a profile meta link?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109739836062889277",
			"parentId": "109739807907622181",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109739836062889277",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-23T18:03:30.240Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@patak\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>patak</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://m.nintendojo.fr/@meduz\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>meduz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@elk\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>elk</span></a></span> forgive my armchair design idea but I think it’s pretty close to great as-is. I’d just remove the follower count minimums.</p><p>Then for groups keep the only small avatars for everyone and sort the avatars in the group first by if they have avatar/cover image (and then maybe by follower count too?).</p><p>For singles/non-groups, only show large previews if a user has avatar/cover image.</p><p>(feel free to ignore me, too 😅—still loving it either way)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109740517049498525",
			"parentId": "109739836062889277",
			"url": "https://m.webtoo.ls/@patak/109740516994043081",
			"author": {
				"name": "patak",
				"url": "https://m.webtoo.ls/@patak",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/467/347/427/647/201/original/3506ee2939de8823.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-23T20:56:40.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.nintendojo.fr/@meduz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>meduz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://m.webtoo.ls/@elk\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>elk</span></a></span> I think we should still show some big cards for grouped notifications. There are a lot of times when people follow you in groups because of a post was shared a lot. Let's try a new algorithm for grouping that stills uses the followers count but removes the minimum limit and see how it works.</p><p>Elk will now order each group according to who has a header first (giving priority to folks that did setup their account), and who has more followers second. Then it shows the first one of the group (if it has a header) as a big card, no matter how many followers it has. If only one remains and it has a header, it is also expanded as a big card. If not, the remaining are shown as a group of avatars in a single line.</p><p><a href=\"https://github.com/elk-zone/elk/pull/1408\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/elk-zone/elk/pull/1</span><span class=\"invisible\">408</span></a></p><p>You can switch to Elks' canary release and see how it works for you before it hits the alpha channel at <a href=\"https://main.elk.zone\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">main.elk.zone</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109740696617989345",
			"parentId": "109740517049498525",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109740696617989345",
			"author": {
